msgid "Install {title}"
msgstr "Suiteáil {title}"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Install {title}\n"
"\n"
"In a box, these parts of {title} won't work:\n"
"{notes}\n"
"A .deb file can't go on the system. For everything to work, look for {title} as an .rpm file or in Bazaar, the app store.\n"
"\n"
"{setup}: puts it in a box anyway, without those parts."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil {title}\n"
"\n"
"I mbosca, ní oibreoidh na codanna seo de {title}:\n"
"{notes}\n"
"Ní féidir comhad .deb a chur ar an gcóras. Le go n-oibreoidh gach rud, cuardaigh {title} mar chomhad .rpm nó i mBazaar, an siopa aipeanna.\n"
"\n"
"{setup}: cuireann sé i mbosca é ar aon nós, gan na codanna sin."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Install {title}\n"
"\n"
"It comes from {maker}'s own download source, which is added to the system so {title} keeps updating. Needs your password and a restart.\n"
"\n"
"To connect, you need a {maker} account."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil {title}\n"
"\n"
"Tagann sé ó fhoinse íoslódála {maker} féin, a chuirtear leis an gcóras ionas go leanfaidh {title} á nuashonrú. Teastaíonn d'fhocal faire agus atosú.\n"
"\n"
"Chun ceangal, teastaíonn cuntas {maker} uait."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Install {title}\n"
"\n"
"Recommended: Add to the system. In a box, these parts of {title} won't work:\n"
"{notes}\n"
"On the system, everything works. Needs your password and a restart.\n"
"\n"
"Or {setup}: puts it in a separate box. It's easier to remove, but those parts won't work."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil {title}\n"
"\n"
"Molta: Cuir leis an gcóras. I mbosca, ní oibreoidh na codanna seo de {title}:\n"
"{notes}\n"
"Ar an gcóras, oibríonn gach rud. Teastaíonn d'fhocal faire agus atosú.\n"
"\n"
"Nó {setup}: cuireann sé i mbosca ar leith é. Tá sé níos éasca é a bhaint, ach ní oibreoidh na codanna sin."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Install {title}\n"
"\n"
"{setup}: puts it in a separate box. Your system isn't changed, and Remove Apps takes it out cleanly."
msgstr ""
"Suiteáil {title}\n"
"\n"
"{setup}: cuireann sé i mbosca ar leith é. Ní athraítear do chóras, agus baineann Bain Aipeanna amach go glan é."

